WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Two lines always cross somewhere, right or wrong.

2
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.500
So how do you know your fix is any good?

3
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.750
You take a third bearing.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.825
Look at the diagram.

5
00:00:11.075 --> 00:00:15.925
With real instruments, three lines almost never meet at one exact point.

6
00:00:16.175 --> 00:00:19.300
They make a small triangle, called a cocked hat.

7
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.750
Put your fix in the middle of it.

8
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.150
That triangle is honest.

9
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.925
It’s showing you the size of your error.

10
00:00:27.175 --> 00:00:29.400
A small one means good bearings.

11
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.250
And a big one?

12
00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.000
Something’s wrong.

13
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:41.675
You misidentified a landmark, or misread the compass, or drew a bearing from the wrong side, or forgot a correction.

14
00:00:41.925 --> 00:00:44.300
Don’t average a big triangle.

15
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.250
Find the mistake.

16
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.675
The ideal is three objects about one hundred twenty degrees apart, all around you.
